menuconfig LIB_ZTCS_SECURE_LINK
	bool "Secure link (Noise IK)"
	default n
	---help---
		Terminate Noise_IK_25519_ChaChaPoly_SHA256 against the ground
		station, so MAVLink leaves the aircraft encrypted and
		authenticated. The ground station end is ztcs-mavlink-gateway.

		Needs the PX4 crypto backend for the keystore the keys come
		from, and CONFIG_CRYPTO in the NuttX configuration for SHA-256,
		HMAC, Poly1305 and X25519, and a seeded /dev/random for the
		ephemeral keys. A session key drawn from an unseeded pool is
		worthless whatever the protocol above it.

config LIB_ZTCS_SECURE_LINK_HFS
	bool "Hybrid forward secrecy (ML-KEM-768)"
	depends on LIB_ZTCS_SECURE_LINK
	default n
	---help---
		Add ML-KEM-768 to the handshake beside X25519, so a session
		recorded today is not readable by a quantum computer later.
		The session holds if either half holds.

		Both ends or neither: the protocol name is part of the hash,
		so a station without it cannot open a link from an aircraft
		with it. The ground station end is the gateway's `hfs`
		feature.

		Handshake messages grow to 1394 and 1153 bytes, which the
		radio carries in about 0.45 s each way, once per rekey.
		Transport frames do not change.

config PX4_NOISE_KEM_STACKSIZE
	int "Stack for the KEM worker"
	depends on LIB_ZTCS_SECURE_LINK_HFS
	default 32768
	---help---
		ML-KEM-768 needs far more stack than a syscall has: measured
		at 18.6 KB to generate a keypair and 22.9 KB to decapsulate,
		against the 8 KB a syscall runs on. The handshake therefore
		runs on a thread of its own and the caller waits. One stack
		for the system, rather than raising every task's.

config LIB_ZTCS_SECURE_LINK_IDENTITY_PATH
	string "Signed identity payload"
	depends on LIB_ZTCS_SECURE_LINK
	default "/fs/certs/ztcs-identity"
	---help---
		Where the signed identity payload is cached. It is public and
		checked against the live keys when read, so any persistent
		path will do.
